==English==

===Etymology===
U.S. regional variation of “[[champ#Verb|champ]]” (verb)

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tʃɒmp/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|chŏmp}}, {{IPA|/t͡ʃɔmp/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-chomp.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|chomp|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒmp|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of [[chomping]] {{qualifier|see below}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[bite]] or [[chew]] [[loudly]] or heavily.
#: ''The dog '''chomped''' the treat and swallowed it in one gulp.''
# {{lb|en|computing|transitive|[[Perl]]}} To remove the final character from (a [[text]] [[string]]) if it is a [[newline]] (or, less commonly, some other programmer-specified character).

